# The tree's openrgb-9999 no longer takes its OpenRGB-0.9-udev-check.patch —
# upstream master moved the code. ::pwr carries a fixed fork of the live
# ebuild (plus the Gainward RTX 5070 Ti detector), so mask only the ::gentoo
# copy and let the pwr one win.
=app-misc/openrgb-9999::gentoo

# GitHub regenerated the gh.tar.gz for cuda-pathfinder-1.6.0 (size drifted 19
# bytes) and ::stuff's Manifest predates that — every fetch dies on a digest
# mismatch. ::pwr carries the same ebuild with a refreshed Manifest; mask the
# stale copy so the fixed one wins (2026-08-08, same pattern as openrgb above).
=dev-python/cuda-pathfinder-1.6.0::stuff

# src_unpack loops `for f in "${A}"` — quoted, so with more than one enabled
# PYTHON_TARGETS both wheels arrive as a single word and cp dies. ::pwr
# carries the fixed copy (2026-08-08).
=dev-python/cuda-tile-bin-1.5.0::stuff

# Slot conflicts against packages the image already has installed. Same failure
# mode as nvidia/package.mask/ml-stack-pins: without these, 'pkgs' merges
# nothing at all instead of merging what it can.
# sys-apps/usbguard-1.1.3 requires <dev-cpp/catch-3
>=dev-cpp/catch-3
# app-emulation/qemu-10.2.3 requires ~sys-firmware/edk2-bin-202408
>sys-firmware/edk2-bin-202408
# 2026-11-07: libfmt-12.2.0 (::gentoo) and cudnn-9.28.0.42 (::stuff) change a subslot that
# pool gpkgs the images have INSTALLED were built against: spdlog-1.17.0-2, android-tools-36.0.1-2,
# mangohud-0.8.4-1 and caffe2-9999-10 carry libfmt:0/12.1.0=, cudnn-frontend-1.28.0-3 carries
# cudnn:0/9.27.0=. With --usepkg the slot-operator rebuild selects the SAME stale gpkg as the
# "rebuild" (the installed instance and the pool file are one build id), which pulls the old
# library back in: two libfmt / two cudnn in one slot and pass 1 aborts (nvidiahard, probed
# 2026-11-07: --usepkg-exclude on every consumer resolves it, but that is a 3 h caffe2 source
# build for a libfmt point release). The host builds first (same lineage): hold until its
# rebuilt gpkgs are copied into the pool (build-pipeline.md §35), then lift both lines together.
>=dev-libs/libfmt-12.2
>=dev-libs/cudnn-9.28

# libddcutil aborts its client when a monitor answers VCP xDF with a version
# outside the MCCS spec — this host's PG34WCDN says 2.18 — so ddcui dies with
# SIGABRT the moment the feature view opens. ::pwr carries the fix
# (project_ddcutil_fork). Unlike the entries around it this mask is NOT pinned
# to a version, and deliberately so: ::gentoo shipped 2.2.7 four hours before
# the ::pwr fork of the SAME version existed, the host merged the unpatched
# build, and 'emerge --update' will never swap a package that differs only by
# repository — it ran broken for two days (2026-09-23, fixed with --newrepo).
# A version-pinned mask would let the next ::gentoo release repeat that
# silently. ddcui itself needs no fork: the bug is entirely in libddcutil.
# Cost of this shape: ::pwr must be bumped for every ddcutil release, or the
# image stays on the forked version. 'pwrup check app-misc/ddcutil' is the
# signal.
app-misc/ddcutil::gentoo

# Same GitHub-regenerated-tarball failure as 1.6.0 above, now on 1.7.0 (size
# drifted 8 bytes: 3192054 -> 3192062). Content is unchanged - the tarball's
# pax header still carries commit 1ca15a3d, which is what the
# cuda-pathfinder-v1.7.0 tag points to - so only the gzip stream moved. ::pwr
# carries the same ebuild with a refreshed Manifest (2026-08-24).
=dev-python/cuda-pathfinder-1.7.0::stuff

# net-libs/webkit-gtk 2.54.0 (-r411 :4.1, -r601 :6) is stable (seen 2026-10-03); every hard
# image has 2.52.6 in both slots and binpkgs of it. Each bump is a multi-hour
# rebuild of two slots that nothing in the images asks for. Hold on 2.52.x; lift
# deliberately (security release) together with a binpkg build.
>=net-libs/webkit-gtk-2.54

# ::stuff splits httpx2 2.13.1 into httpx2 + httpcore2 without a blocker against the
# combined ::gentoo httpx2 (which ships the httpcore2 module itself): pkgs merged
# httpcore2 first and died on file collisions with the installed httpx2-2.10.0,
# taking httpx2 and openai-3.24.0 with it (2026-10-03). ::gentoo's httpx2-2.13.1
# satisfies openai's >=2.12.0 on its own.
dev-python/httpx2::stuff
dev-python/httpcore2::stuff

# 2026-11-01 -> lifted 2026-11-07: ffmpeg-chromium-155.0.8059.85 was unfetchable (404 on
# distfiles.gentoo.org, the googlesource '+archive' fallback regenerated per request and
# never matched the Manifest), so it and opera-developer-140.0.6066.0 (the only image
# package with CHROMIUM_VERSION=155) were masked here. ::gentoo has since moved the
# SRC_URI to deps.gentoo.zip and refreshed the Manifest (11643376 bytes); 'ebuild ... fetch'
# verified the digest on 2026-11-07, so both masks are gone. Lesson: the opera mask was
# pinned to 140.0.6066.0 and rotted the moment ::gentoo bumped to 140.0.6072.0 - @installed
# then pulled the unmasked 140.0.6072.0 and died on the still-masked ffmpeg-chromium:155.
# A hold on a package that tracks another must cover the range (>=), not one version.
